The attached image illustrates that Nano-11 enhances the transport and uptake of antigens by cells in the draining lymph nodes. Panel (A) shows flow cytometry plots indicating a higher percentage of OVA-positive cells and increased mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) for OVA when complexed with Nano-11 (OVA+N11) compared to OVA alone or OVA with aluminum hydroxide (OVA+AH). Panel (B) quantitatively confirms that Nano-11 formulations result in significantly higher MFI of OVA per cell in the draining lymph nodes on both day 1 and day 2. Panel (C) demonstrates that Nano-11 specifically increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, indicating targeted antigen delivery to key antigen-presenting cells crucial for initiating immune responses.